<title>UK: Signs of rain in England soon, but may be light.</title>
<headline>Signs of rain in England soon, but may be light.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>There are definite signs of rain in England over the next few days, a spokesman for Britain's Meteorological Office said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The question is how much will fall in the most needy places,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>There was still a possibility that East Anglia, where grain farmers are crying out for rain, would only get light rainfall, which would not be enough to help crops facing damage from the lack of moisture, he said.</p>
<p>There has been rain in places in England in recent days, but the amounts involved had been no more than &quot;dribs and drabs&quot;, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The total rain over the past three to four days had amounted to around one millimetre, which he described as &quot;nowhere near enough&quot;.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
